{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20278",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 3.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.02,
      "end_seconds": 8.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.08,
      "end_seconds": 14.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a blister."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.29,
      "end_seconds": 17.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.5,
      "end_seconds": 29.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux. I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for my mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.24,
      "end_seconds": 32.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.18,
      "end_seconds": 39.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.54,
      "end_seconds": 44.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.59,
      "end_seconds": 50.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "It's been like this since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.77,
      "end_seconds": 54.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Have you had being worried about scarring?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.44,
      "end_seconds": 58.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Actually, yeah. Two weeks, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.92,
      "end_seconds": 59.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.4,
      "end_seconds": 68.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "I've also had a stinging pain. About stinging pain, it's all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.78,
      "end_seconds": 72.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "What about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.21,
      "end_seconds": 75.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.79,
      "end_seconds": 85.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chemical exposure, burn on the face or numbness at the burn?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.91,
      "end_seconds": 88.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "None of those, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.42,
      "end_seconds": 94.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Right, right. Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.51,
      "end_seconds": 97.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.69,
      "end_seconds": 101.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Right, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.3,
      "end_seconds": 104.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.22,
      "end_seconds": 108.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.08,
      "end_seconds": 113.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Yes, kiwi. I get an itchy mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.69,
      "end_seconds": 118.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.03,
      "end_seconds": 123.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for five years. Yes, depression."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.15,
      "end_seconds": 129.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Alright, acid reflux, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.7,
      "end_seconds": 143.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.7,
      "end_seconds": 149.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.75,
      "end_seconds": 151.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.96,
      "end_seconds": 155.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.4,
      "end_seconds": 172.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.0,
      "end_seconds": 176.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.66,
      "end_seconds": 183.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.21,
      "end_seconds": 199.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.78,
      "end_seconds": 216.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 123 over 81, pulse is 77 beats a minute, temperature is 36.4 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.85,
      "end_seconds": 222.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.11,
      "end_seconds": 225.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.64,
      "end_seconds": 247.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "There is a five-centimetre area of redness with an intact blister on the left forearm, and it blanches and is painful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.14,
      "end_seconds": 255.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.12,
      "end_seconds": 303.34,
      "duration_seconds": 30.22,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? This looks most like a superficial partial-thickness burn. I'll start you on paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. That should help with burn pain. Cool the area under running water for twenty minutes and cover it with a non-stick dressing, and leave the blister alone. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.4,
      "end_seconds": 322.12,
      "duration_seconds": 16.72,
      "text": "Come back or go to emergency straight away if the burn becomes smelly, spreads or you get a fever. Let's plan a check in three days. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.71,
      "end_seconds": 326.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}